  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sri Venkatachalapathy Rice And Sago ... vs Commissioner Of Food Safety on 3 January, 2024 Author: S.M.Subramaniam Bench: S.M.Subramaniam WP.No.6897/2020 In The High Court Of Judicature At Madras Dated: 03.01.2024 Coram: The Honourable Mr.Justice S.M.Subramaniam W.P.No.6897 of 2020 & WMP.Nos.8229 & 8231 of 2020 Sri Venkatachalapathy Rice and Sago Factory, rep. by its Proprietress Tmt.K.Susila, Thandavarayapuram, Attur Taluk, Salem District. ...Petitioner vs. 1.Commissioner of Food Safety, No.359, Anna Salai, V Floor, Dms Office Building, Dms Campus, Teynampet, Chennai 600 006. 2.Designated Officer, Food Safety and Drug Administration Department, Salem District, Salem-1 . 3.Food Safety Officer, Attur Town, Salem District. 4.S.Mariappan, Formerly Designated Officer, Food Safety and Drug Administration Department, Salem District, Salem-1. .. Respondents 1/9 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis Sri Venkatachalapathy Rice And Sago ... vs Commissioner Of Food Safety on 3 January, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/60519769/ 1 WP.No PRAYER: Writ Petition filed under Article 226 of the Constitution of praying to issue a Writ of Certiorarified Mandamus, calling for the records relating to the Proceedings in D.Dis.No.9464/2018/S6/FSSA Da 20-03-2019 and R.No.0085/2019/S9/FSSA Dated 11-06-2019 on the file of the 1st respondent herein and quash the same and consequently dir the 1st respondent herein to issue orders to withdraw the prosecutio launched against the petitioner herein in S.T.C.No.623 of 2019 dated 03.05.2019 on the file of the Judicial Magistrate No.1, Attur pre-em the directions issued by this Hon'ble Court in W.P.No.11 of 2019 dt.11.02.2019. For Petitioners : Mr.V.R.Rajasekaran For R1 to R3 : Mr.G.Krishna Raja, Additional Government Pleader For R4 : No appearance",
    "facts": "The writ petition was disposed of on 11.02.2019 considering the objections filed by the petitioner as an appeal under Section 46(4) of the Food Safety and https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis Standards Act, 2006.",
    "arguments": "4.The learned counsel for the petitioner mainly contended that even before the receipt of the orders of this Court, the objections filed by the petitioner and the appeal was disposed of by the Authority, thereby, depriving the petitioner to submit further objections."
  },
